                    {
                        "sense_id": "7e8800fb-5ed2-3ae1-8231-4d53068acd79",
                        "entry_id": "f58c20fd-23fb-3015-8c02-10457b8dbfd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "an aquatic vortex, maelstrom, large whirlpool; especially a tidal vortex"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2f94654-08d1-4dad-b035-02100cead3ee",
                                "sense_id": "7e8800fb-5ed2-3ae1-8231-4d53068acd79",
                                "text": "1769, Charles Papillon, Algemeen en beredenerent woordenboek der natuurlyke historie, tr. by Valmont de Bomare from French, publ. by Abraham Blussé & son, page 846.\nDe grootſte maalſtroom die men kent, is die van de Noorweegſche Zee, men verzekert dat hy meer als twintig uuren in omtrek beſlaat; hy zwelgt gedurende zes uuren alles in wat hy in zynen omtrek ontmoet, Water, Walviſſchen en Schepen, en hy geeft vervolgens, gedurende dezelve uitgeſtrektheid van tyd alles weder uit, wat hy ingezwolgen heeft.",
                                "translation": "The largest maelstrom, that is known, is the one of the Norwegian Sea, one insists that it covers more than twenty hours in circumference; it swallows during six hours everything in that it encounters in its circumference, water, whales and schips, and it subsequently reemits everything again during that same expanse of time, what it has swallowed in.",
                                "english": "The largest maelstrom, that is known, is the one of the Norwegian Sea, one insists that it covers more than twenty hours in circumference; it swallows during six hours everything in that it encounters in its circumference, water, whales and schips, and it subsequently reemits everything again during that same expanse of time, what it has swallowed in."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b6eff89-0698-3908-b2e8-63fe7826d1ac",
                        "entry_id": "f58c20fd-23fb-3015-8c02-10457b8dbfd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "any kind of vortex"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "653e6f96-9365-40a0-874f-acaae46bd53d",
                                "sense_id": "3b6eff89-0698-3908-b2e8-63fe7826d1ac",
                                "text": "Novalis (Georg Philipp Friedrich Freiherr von Hardenberg), \"Wat zou ik zonder U geweest zijn\", tr. by Jan Wit from German, couplet 2.\nIk werd verteerd door wild verlangen, / door 's levens maalstroom weggevaagd.",
                                "translation": "I was being devoured by savage longing, / swept away by the maelstrom of life.",
                                "english": "I was being devoured by savage longing, / swept away by the maelstrom of life."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
